WEBVTT

resistance-03-1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.788
Previously: one person wants to hold on
to the past; another wants to strive for

resistance-03-2
00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:08.360
the future. In reality, there is only one
chair.

resistance-03-3
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:15.120
This time: why are those who hold on and
those who strive both anxious?

resistance-03-4
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.680
Episode 3: Those Who Hold On, Those Who
Strive

resistance-03-5
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.701
Imagine a university street dance club.
Its president has led it for three years.

resistance-03-6
00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:32.284
The club’s style, performance roster, and
‘who has the final say’ are already

resistance-03-7
00:00:32.284 --> 00:00:32.760
settled.

resistance-03-8
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.573
A new member joined just six months ago.
She wants to dance in her own style and

resistance-03-9
00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:39.980
get on the roster for the year-end show.

resistance-03-10
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.900
Only the final line of the roster remains
‘to be decided.’

resistance-03-11
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.450
This series places them in two positions.

resistance-03-12
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.647
What they want — Holding on: for
established identities, status, and

resistance-03-13
00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:57.408
arrangements of recognition to continue.
Striving: a self and a position not yet

resistance-03-14
00:00:57.408 --> 00:00:59.570
realized, but believed to be what ought
to be.

resistance-03-15
00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.101
In the club — Holding on: ‘I am the
president’; style and roster follow the

resistance-03-16
00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:06.490
old rules. Striving: ‘I should be onstage
too,’ dancing in my own style.

resistance-03-17
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.705
Direction in time — Holding on: toward
what already exists. Striving: toward

resistance-03-18
00:01:09.705 --> 00:01:10.720
what does not yet exist.

resistance-03-19
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.460
The author’s distinction

resistance-03-20
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.100
‘Could we add a piece I choreographed to
the year-end show?’

resistance-03-21
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:25.401
For the president, this question makes it
uncertain whether the arrangement can

resistance-03-22
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:26.340
stay as it is.

resistance-03-23
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.670
‘The roster is ranked by attendance. That
has always been the rule.’

resistance-03-24
00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:38.290
For the new member, this answer makes it
uncertain whether she will be recognized.

resistance-03-25
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:45.267
The action one side takes for its own
security is precisely the uncertainty the

resistance-03-26
00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:46.680
other must face.

resistance-03-27
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.080
Each side has its own anxiety and its own
way of managing it.

resistance-03-28
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.640
And their anxieties are connected,
driving each other in a recurring loop.

resistance-03-29
00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.667
Author’s OSIPP draft, 2B(i): ‘Once
subjects within the order are

resistance-03-30
00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:02.263
differentiated into these two positions,
their respective forms of anxiety and the

resistance-03-31
00:02:02.263 --> 00:02:04.100
ways they manage it become correlated in
a recursive way.’

resistance-03-32
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.050
This series’ proposition

resistance-03-33
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.990
So both sides begin to act.

resistance-03-34
00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.550
The president explains, screens, and
adjusts the rules: ‘New choreography is

resistance-03-35
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.310
fine, but show it at a regular meeting
first.’

resistance-03-36
00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.744
The new member looks for words the other
side understands: ‘This piece could help

resistance-03-37
00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.550
the club place in a competition.’

resistance-03-38
00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:33.546
Pause for a moment: in a relationship in
your life right now, are you more like

resistance-03-39
00:02:33.546 --> 00:02:37.000
the one holding on or the one striving?

resistance-03-40
00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:44.410
Take care: these are two positions, not
two kinds of people.

resistance-03-41
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:48.964
The same president goes to the student
council to seek funding and rehearsal

resistance-03-42
00:02:48.964 --> 00:02:51.960
space for the club. There, he is the one
striving.

resistance-03-43
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:58.922
One person can even occupy both positions
at once: holding on to some things while

resistance-03-44
00:02:58.922 --> 00:03:00.620
striving for others.

resistance-03-45
00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.020
Another guardrail: position does not
determine who is right or wrong.

resistance-03-46
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:11.800
What is being held on to may be unfair
privilege, or something worth protecting.

resistance-03-47
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.886
What is being sought may be overdue
justice, or merely a chance to sit in

resistance-03-48
00:03:16.886 --> 00:03:18.210
that chair oneself.

resistance-03-49
00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:23.567
For now, this series sets aside judgments
of right and wrong to examine one thing:

resistance-03-50
00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:26.050
how both sides’ anxieties form a loop.

resistance-03-51
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.990
This episode’s comparison card (take a
screenshot)

resistance-03-52
00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.123
The position of holding on — President:
style, roster, ‘who has the final say.’

resistance-03-53
00:03:33.123 --> 00:03:34.670
Already realized; wants it to continue.

resistance-03-54
00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.015
The position of striving — New member:
wants to go onstage and dance in her own

resistance-03-55
00:03:38.015 --> 00:03:40.090
style. Not yet realized; believes it
ought to be.

resistance-03-56
00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.031
Both sides are anxious — A proposal, a
reply. One side’s action = the other

resistance-03-57
00:03:44.031 --> 00:03:45.030
side’s uncertainty.

resistance-03-58
00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:50.283
Relational positions — At the student
council, the president becomes the one

resistance-03-59
00:03:50.283 --> 00:03:53.600
striving. These are positions, not fixed
people.

resistance-03-60
00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:00.310
Anxiety is not a problem belonging to
just one side.

resistance-03-61
00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.150
It passes back and forth between the two
positions.

resistance-03-62
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:07.940
The chair is still there.

resistance-03-63
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.600
Next time:

resistance-03-64
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:15.220
Can Order Feel Anxious Too?

resistance-03-65
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.430
This is UjiBricks.
